    "report": "Archiving is finished and committed as `1aa5302` on `main`, the current branch. Nothing is pushed. I committed to `main` because you asked for the current branch; the usual practice is to branch off a default branch first, so say if you'd rather have that.\n\n**What the previous developer left:** the aggregate behaviour, the command handler, the persistence and a unit spec. It was missing the route, the module wiring, the list filter and any e2e coverage. I kept their work and built on it.\n\n**What I added:**\n- `POST /v1/conversations/{id}/archive`, answered `202` and followed at `/operations/{id}`, like `read`. The command is wired into the Messaging module.\n- The summary read model now carries `archived`: true when the reader archived the conversation and no message was written after it.\n- `GET /conversations/mine` drops archived rows. `GET /conversations/unread` still counts them, and `GET /conversations/{id}` still reads them.\n- Other readers are unaffected, because the archive is stored per reader.\n- Refusals: a non-reader gets `ERROR` with `NotFound`, and a caller who isn't signed in gets `401`.\n- E2e cases for the list, unread, read-by-id, re-archiving, a new message bringing the conversation back, and both refusals.\n\n**Verification:** typecheck, `check:conventions`, lint, `format:check`, unit tests (156 suites, 1052 tests) and the e2e suite (114 suites, 610 tests) all pass. I didn't start a server, so port 4471 is unused. I also didn't run `clean-ddd knowledge`.\n\n**Choices I made where the request was open:**\n- \"A new message\" means any stored message, including one later hidden by an upheld report. The aggregate already counts hidden messages as part of the conversation, so I kept that.\n- The archive is shown as a flag on the summary rather than as a separate query, so `unread` and `mine` read the same data and can't drift.",
